# Design Start

<!-- prism:design-start-contract:v1 -->

Prepare, preview, and, after explicit confirmation, write one feature-only
transition:

`ready-for-design` + `designer` -> `in-design` + `designer`

## Usage

`$design-start [F-XXX]`

Resolve `[F-XXX]` to exactly one existing feature file. Accept only the exact
source pair above; do not infer a transition from another status or owner.
Read `knowledge/wiki/SCHEMA.md`, `knowledge/wiki/LIFECYCLE.md`, `index.md`, the feature, linked context, and
workspace identity. The feature's declared apps define the design scope.

When available, use the read-only probe:

```text
prism wiki transition-preflight F-XXX [path] --action design-start --json
```

Require envelope schema 1, command facts, capability version 2 with an
action-specific `design-start` surface, transition version 1, target owner
`designer`, and a consistent snapshot. A version string alone is insufficient;
unsupported capability falls back to direct-file checks. The preflight is
copy-only and never authorizes a write.

Before confirmation, verify the exact feature path, source fields, app scope,
advisory state, and any active `revalidation` domains. An active `specification`
domain blocks this downstream start until PO verifies it; an active `design`
domain may be worked by the designer and does not pretend that design evidence
already exists. Designer-owned open questions may remain while design starts.
Pending advisory review is an unresolved blocker; use the existing board-review
or explicit skip policy where that policy applies. Do not invent a new waiver.

Show the proposed `status` change, unchanged owner, evidence, and complete write
set. Reread the source and context immediately before asking for confirmation and
again after confirmation. On confirmation, update the feature, matching index row,
and log entry. Cancellation or decline leaves all files unchanged. If a multi-file
write is partial, report exact changes and stop for fresh recovery; no transaction
is implied.

Return the observed source and destination fields and the design-scope evidence.
This action starts work; it does not prove design completeness or development
readiness.
